      "content": "I totally get not wanting to deal with the ER bill, but lower right pain plus nausea is exactly how appendicitis starts, and it can turn dangerous fast. Gas or a heavy burrito usually causes more central or upper belly discomfort, not that specific sharp spot. Please don't take antacids—they won't help if it's your appendix, and they can mask symptoms. If the pain gets worse when you press on it, or moves toward your belly button, that's a huge red flag. Go get checked; it's better to be told it's gas than to risk a rupture.",
